# Act 2, chapter 5 "Siblings": the district around West City (areas from log4/gen_ch5.py, world 4). The Red Fangs, a
# street gang, have moved into the twins' hideout (the old warehouse at the docks); a man in a long coat paid them to.
# Flags: 293 vendor, 294 Big Ox beaten (his death script), 295 stash recovered, 296 medal returned, 297 riverside cache,
# 298 delivery returned, 299 docks cache, 387 curator asked, 388 clerk asked, 389 den intro.
list ch5_vendor
if_flag 295 vendor_after
if_flag 293 vendor_again
set_flag 293
narrate Street vendor: You two! Keep walking, before those Red Fang creeps see you talking to me.
say lapis.1 Red Fangs? Since when does that bunch of losers run the circus lot?
narrate Street vendor: Since last week. They take a cut of every sale. And last night they moved into the old warehouse down at the docks.
say lazuli.0 The warehouse. Our warehouse.
say lapis.2 Everything we own is in there.
narrate Street vendor: Then you can kiss it goodbye. Their boss is a mountain called Big Ox. Out past the river, on the island by the docks.
say lazuli.3 Big Ox. Of course he is.
journal Take back the warehouse from the {c07}Red Fangs{c02}
stop
label vendor_again
narrate Street vendor: The docks are south of the city, over the river. Big Ox doesn't leave the warehouse.
stop
label vendor_after
narrate Street vendor: You ran the Red Fangs out? Ha! First good day I've had all month. The lemonade's on me. Just this once.
list ch5_den
set_flag 389
set_flag 293
narrate The old warehouse. Their mattresses have been thrown in a heap. Someone has spray-painted a red fang on the wall.
narrate Big Ox: Well, well. The little pickpockets came home.
say lapis.1 You're in our place, Ox. Get out.
narrate Big Ox: Your place? Funny. A man paid me good money to take it off you. Said to wait here and see what you'd do.
say lazuli.0 What man?
narrate Big Ox: Doesn't matter. Boys! Teach these two some manners.
journal Defeat {c07}Big Ox{c02}
do call 47; call 51 0
list ch5_stash
if_flag 295 stash_done
unless_flag 294 stash_guarded
set_flag 295
narrate Behind the crates, under a loose board: the twins' tin box. Still there.
say lapis.2 Every zeni. They didn't even find it.
narrate Next to it, a crate the Red Fangs filled with their haul: Z-Mart cartons, and a medal in a glass case.
say lazuli.0 Somebody's going to want those back.
narrate Big Ox (from the floor): Old guy... long coat. Paid in cash. Said you two were... special. That's all I know. I swear.
say lazuli.3 Lapis. The man in the coat again.
say lapis.1 Then let him watch. We're done hiding from him.
do call 129 11 1; call 129 2 2
narrate Got a Senzu Bean and two Sodas. The stolen goods are with the twins now.
journal Head back to West City
run ch5_check
stop
label stash_guarded
narrate The stash is back here. But not with Big Ox standing over it.
stop
label stash_done
narrate Nothing left behind the crates.
list docks_dome
if_flag 299 dome_done
set_flag 299
narrate The dome house is locked. Lazuli picks the lock in four seconds.
narrate Inside: a Red Fang lookout's stash. A carton of milk and a cherry soda.
do call 129 0 1; call 129 4 1
stop
label dome_done
narrate The lookout's dome is empty now.
list cache_river
if_flag 297 river_empty
set_flag 297
narrate A rowboat pulled up under the trees. In the bottom, a forgotten thermos of tea.
do call 129 1 1
stop
label river_empty
narrate An old rowboat. Nothing else.
# ---------- Z-Mart (flag 388 asked, 298 done)
list zmart_clerk
if_flag 298 clerk_done
unless_flag 295 clerk_ask
set_flag 298
narrate Z-Mart clerk: Our delivery! The Red Fangs took it right off the truck. Where did you find this?
say lapis.2 Lying around. Some people just leave things anywhere.
narrate Z-Mart clerk: Well... thank you. Take these, on the house. And hey, if you ever need a job...
say lazuli.1 We'll pass.
do call 129 3 2
narrate Got two Vanilla Sodas.
stop
label clerk_ask
set_flag 388
narrate Z-Mart clerk: Sorry, we're nearly out of everything. The Red Fangs hijacked our delivery truck yesterday.
narrate Z-Mart clerk: And someone took three watches off the counter this morning. Kids these days.
say lapis.2 Shocking.
stop
label clerk_done
narrate Z-Mart clerk: Welcome to Z-Mart! You two again? ...Did you just put something in your pocket?
# ---------- West City Museum (flag 387 asked, 296 done)
list museum_curator
if_flag 296 curator_done
unless_flag 295 curator_ask
set_flag 296
narrate Curator: The medal! The Red Ribbon Army's own service medal, back in its case. I could kiss you both.
say lazuli.3 Please don't.
narrate Curator: Then take this. Old army rations... the soldiers swore by them.
do call 129 11 1
narrate Got a Senzu Bean.
set_flag 461
narrate Curator: And next week, the gala! Commander Red's own ruby, the Ribbon Ruby. It's locked in the storeroom until then.
narrate Curator: We've hired a guard and everything. He sits by the storeroom door all day.
say lazuli.0 A ruby. How big?
narrate Curator: Big enough to buy this museum twice! Not that it's for sale, of course.
journal (Optional) The {c07}Ribbon Ruby{c02} in the museum storeroom
stop
label curator_ask
set_flag 387
narrate Curator: Welcome to the West City Museum. I'm afraid our best piece is missing: a Red Ribbon Army service medal.
narrate Curator: A gang broke in two nights ago. The police say it's "not a priority". Hmph.
stop
label curator_done
set_flag 461
narrate Curator: Every school class in West City comes to see that medal. Thanks to you, it's still here.
narrate Curator: Come back for the gala next week. The Ribbon Ruby! Our guard hasn't left that storeroom door all day.
list museum_exhibit
narrate The Red Ribbon Army exhibit. Uniforms, a rusted rifle, a photograph of a burned-out headquarters.
narrate The plaque reads: "Destroyed in a single day. The army's chief scientist was never found."
say lazuli.0 Somebody built all this... and one kid knocked it down.
say lapis.1 Never found, huh? Bet he's somewhere sulking about it.
# ---------- side job "Lost Brother" (log4/gen_more.py; flags 464 asked, 465 reunited)
list lost_boy
if_flag 465 boy_after
set_flag 464
narrate Little boy: (sniffling) My sister said wait right here. She said she'd be right back. That was before lunch.
say lazuli.0 What does she look like?
narrate Little boy: Yellow hair. Like yours. She's really bossy.
say lapis.2 Sounds familiar.
say lazuli.3 Lapis.
narrate Little boy: We were going to the river to see the boats...
journal Find the lost boy's sister (the river?)
stop
label boy_after
narrate Little boy: My sister found me! She said two scary teenagers told her where I was. Thanks, scary teenagers!
list lost_sister
if_flag 465 sister_after
unless_flag 464 sister_alone
set_flag 465
narrate Girl: Have you seen a little boy? This tall, yellow hair, won't stop talking? I turned around for one minute...
say lazuli.1 The circus lot. He's still waiting where you told him to.
narrate Girl: Oh, thank goodness. He never listens to anyone, except when it's the one time he shouldn't.
say lapis.1 You left him alone with the Red Fangs around?
narrate Girl: I know. I know! I'm going. Thank you, both of you!
narrate She presses a bottle into Lazuli's hands and runs for the bridge.
say lazuli.0 Lapis. Remember the rule?
say lapis.2 Never split up. I remember. I made it up.
say lazuli.3 You did not. I did.
do call 129 3 1
narrate Got a Vanilla Soda.
stop
label sister_alone
narrate Girl: (looking up and down the riverbank) Sorry, I can't talk, I'm looking for someone!
stop
label sister_after
narrate Girl: He's sitting on my feet so I can't leave again. It's working.
# ---------- the Ribbon Ruby (flags 461 heard of it, 462 Hercule's show, 463 taken, 466 storeroom arrival, 467 stashed)
list museum_guard
if_flag 463 guard_after
if_flag 462 guard_show
narrate Museum guard: That door says STAFF ONLY, kids. And I'm the staff.
narrate Museum guard: Nobody goes in there till the gala. Not with the ruby back there.
stop
label guard_show
narrate Museum guard: (nose against the window, watching the street) Is that... Hercule? Doing push-ups? On the museum steps?
stop
label guard_after
narrate Museum guard: Back to my post. Nothing ever happens in this museum. Thank goodness.
list storeroom_door
if_flag 463 door_done
unless_flag 461 door_plain
unless_flag 462 door_guarded
narrate The guard has his back to the door, glued to the window. Lazuli has the lock open in six seconds.
say lazuli.0 Stay close. And don't touch anything you can't carry.
do call 120 20; call 119 4 46 1 140 256; call 121 20
stop
label door_plain
narrate A tall double door in the back wall. STAFF ONLY. Locked.
stop
label door_guarded
narrate A tall double door marked STAFF ONLY. The guard on his stool beside it hasn't looked away once.
say lapis.1 We need him looking somewhere else.
stop
label door_done
narrate STAFF ONLY. Locked again, as if nothing ever happened.
list ch5_storeroom
set_flag 466
narrate The museum's storeroom. Statues, crates, sheets over everything. And a night guard with a flashlight.
narrate His beam sweeps the middle of the room, slow and steady. The statues along the walls throw long shadows.
say lazuli.0 Along the walls. Stay in the shadows. The case is at the far end.
journal Take the {c07}Ribbon Ruby{c02} without being seen
do call 47; call 51 0
list storeroom_beam
narrate The flashlight beam swings straight into Lapis's face.
narrate Night guard: Hey! Who's back there? This area is off limits!
say lapis.2 Sorry! Looking for the bathroom!
narrate The twins are out the door before he gets off his stool. Back to the hall, and try again.
do call 120 20; call 119 4 45 1 112 144; call 121 20
list storeroom_guard
narrate Night guard: (sweeping the beam, humming) ...Nobody here. Nobody ever here...
list ruby_case
if_flag 463 ruby_gone
set_flag 463
narrate A glass case under a sheet. Inside, on red velvet: a ruby the size of a hen's egg.
narrate The card reads: THE RIBBON RUBY. Personal property of Commander Red, Red Ribbon Army. Recovered from the ruins of headquarters.
say lapis.1 That's it? We could sell that for a car. Two cars.
say lazuli.0 We're not selling it.
say lapis.2 Then why are we stealing it?
say lazuli.1 For later. For when we need it. Everybody needs one thing put away for later.
do call 129 28 1
narrate Got the Ribbon Ruby.
journal Get out of the museum with the ruby
stop
label ruby_gone
narrate The empty case. Someone has left a single zeni coin on the velvet.
# ---------- Gero's notes 1 and 2 (item 31 "Gero's Note"; flags 520 / 521; all ten -> notes_done in act3_world)
list note_park
if_flag 520 npark_read
set_flag 520
narrate Under the park bench, a page torn from a notebook. Small, careful handwriting.
narrate "Observation, day four. The boy steals. The girl decides what is worth stealing. Neither ever lets the other out of sight."
say lapis.1 Somebody's been taking notes on us.
say lazuli.0 Keep it.
do call 129 31 1
run notes_check
stop
label npark_read
narrate Just a park bench.
list note_museum
if_flag 521 nmus_read
set_flag 521
narrate A notebook page, dropped behind the uniform case. The same small handwriting.
narrate "Visited the exhibit. They have my lab coat behind glass. They spelled my name wrong. Let them keep looking in the wrong place."
say lazuli.0 It's the same writing as the page in the park.
say lapis.1 Somebody who used to work for the Red Ribbon Army. And now he watches kids in parks. Great.
do call 129 31 1
run notes_check
stop
label nmus_read
narrate The uniform case. A red ribbon pinned to a grey coat.
# ---------- exit audit 2026-11-03 (storeroom_side; wc_east_closed is also used in West City at night, 16:1 / 16:2)
list storeroom_side
set_flag 446
narrate A service hatch in the wall, bricked up long ago. Whatever was back there, the museum didn't want it found.
list wc_east_closed
set_flag 442
narrate Police barricades close the road east. A sign hangs from the tape: ROAD CLOSED.
